      "demonstration": "Implemented distinct SLR1 logical ADD WAL containing operation ID, predecessor and delta, with no resulting-counter after-image. Applied-ID, total and last delta share one sealed alternating checkpoint; equal-ID recovery skips replay and conflicting payload is rejected.28commit cuts,28checkpoint cuts,112repeated interruptions,1093reopen-and-duplicate histories per profile; checked signed extrema, maximum-ID disk fixture, resealed gap/overflow/equal-ID disagreement and partial read failures. Independent Python checks1093integer sums,28phase outcomes and a complete4096-byte negative-delta command. Five compiled semantic controls distinguish missing flush, duplicate replay, early output, conflicting ID and defined wrapping addition. Latest same-ID lost-response retry yields17; blind new-ID retry yields24. Exact bounded sequential-client counter semantics only, not arbitrary B+tree redo or external effects.",
